  "v": 11,
  "label": "a copy into a collection where its source's own tombstone holds the identity revives that tombstone under the handle it is bound to",
  "note": "imap syncs INBOX and Archive. Archive holds basic-1@example.org as a tombstone imap binds under handle 4 with a base, its delete not pushed yet (a move out staged since the last sync). A copy from INBOX takes the bare key and revives that row: its binding and base kept, since a binding pins one handle, its delete withdrawn, the item adopting the copied flags and body, so the next sync pushes the flag change against handle 4 and no remove. No create is staged: one under the provisional handle the key derives would rebind the key, which the write refuses, and the copy would park for good (SYNC.md section 7; STORAGE.md sections 9 and 10; live night 2026-11-23)",
